// Title: DHCP Callout DLL Installation
// Sigma ID: 9d3436ef-9476-4c43-acca-90ce06bdf33a
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Dimitrios Slamaris
// Date: 2017-05-15 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, execution, stealth, defense-impairment, T1574.001, T1112
// Description: Detects the installation of a Callout DLL via CalloutDlls and CalloutEnabled parameter in
//   Registry, which can be used to execute code in context of the DHCP server (restart required)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://blog.3or.de/mimilib-dhcp-server-callout-dll-injection.html
//   - https://technet.microsoft.com/en-us/library/cc726884(v=ws.10).aspx
//   - https://msdn.microsoft.com/de-de/library/windows/desktop/aa363389(v=vs.85).aspx
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_dhcp_calloutdll.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Services\\DHCPServer\\Parameters\\CalloutDlls" or RegistryKey endswith "\\Services\\DHCPServer\\Parameters\\CalloutEnabled"
